																		New Writer Seeking Greenlight: The ANTECHAMBER
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malakabyssae" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7107026); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7107026&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607827719" alt="MalakAbyssae" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7107026)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malakabyssae" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7107026); return false;" >MalakAbyssae</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607642724 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Dec 2020 23:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841769">
									

<p>Potential SCP: Several locations around the globe that let psychics access a metaphysical gateway to Hell; allows them to communicate with the dead</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror (existential, graphic)</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong><br />
Standard Order: Class; Containment; Description; Discovery; Exploration Logs and Addenda</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Several locations around the globe allow psychic individuals to access a metaphysical gateway to Hell. This allows them, and by proxy, the Foundation, to communicate with the dead. This SCP is useful, but dangerous: sometimes, something from the other side hitches a ride back to our world&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>Certain locations will periodically undergo <em>Virgil Events</em>. During these events, magically skilled or psionically gifted individuals can access a kind of metaphysical lobby, hosted by a mysterious masked attendant. This Antechamber allows access to a vast, spiritual realm full of dead souls and entities, all in perpetual, self-inflicted agony. Mediums can find and speak to deceased individuals, and gain otherwise unobtainable information for the Foundation.</p>
<p>For example, the Foundation uses this SCP to contact a Chaos Insurgent spy who had been killed while trying to sabotage the Foundation; they able to wring out of the confused spirit the name of his accomplice, still hidden in Foundation ranks.</p>
<p>The Foundation sends many Mediums to explore and document the SCP. But over time, this eats away at their sanity. Moreover, there are occasional <em>Geryon Events</em>, where something will follow the Mediums back into the physical realm, and Foundation soldiers have to deal with them.</p>
<p>The SCP is called the Antechamber because the SCP actually refers to the Lobby-like chamber that Mediums experience when they access the SCP, which allows access to all of Hell.</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong> This article boasts detailed and intense explorations of Hell; it depicts the mental breakdown of those who visit Hell; and it indulges in the <em>occasional</em> badass demon-killing action scene (described via interview logs, as appropriate to an SCP article).</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> The ritual that allows access to this SCP was discovered in a book confiscated from a Marshall, Carter, &amp; Dark shipment.</p>
<p>Thanks to Zyn and Truc Linh for advice in formatting</p>
</div>
